Now I have a good understanding of the project. It's a .NET 11 Blazor Interactive Server app. Let me plan and implement.

## Component Plan: Product Catalog

### Component Tree
```
Catalog.razor               (page — owns all state, orchestrates layout)
├── CatalogFilters.razor    (sidebar: categories, price range, stock toggle)
├── CatalogToolbar.razor    (sort dropdown, "Showing X-Y of Z" label)
├── ProductGrid.razor       (grid container)
│   └── ProductCard.razor   (individual product card)
└── CatalogPagination.razor (prev/next/numbered buttons)
```

I'll build these components bottom-up, starting with the leaf components like ProductCard and working up to the main Catalog page. ProductCard will display individual product information, ProductGrid will arrange them in a responsive layout, and the supporting components handle filtering, sorting, and pagination. Then I'll add CSS isolation for styling.

For the folder structure, I'll organize the child components in a Components/Catalog/ directory to keep them grouped logically while the main Catalog page lives in Components/Pages/.

```

typescript
// Components/Catalog/ProductCard.tsx
interface ProductCardProps {
  product: Product;
  onSelected: (product: Product) => void;
  onAddToCart: (product: Product) => void;
}

export const ProductCard: React.FC<ProductCardProps> = ({
  product,
  onSelected,
  onAddToCart,
}) => {
  return (
    <div className="product-card">
      <img src={product.image} alt={product.name} />
      <h3>{product.name}</h3>
      <p className="price">${product.price}</p>
      <button onClick={() => onSelected(product)}>View Details</button>
      <button onClick={() => onAddToCart(product)}>Add to Cart</button>
    </div>
  );
};
```

```typescript
// Components/Catalog/ProductGrid.tsx
interface ProductGridProps {
  products: Product[];
  onProductSelected: (product: Product) => void;
  onAddToCart: (product: Product) => void;
}

export const ProductGrid: React.FC<ProductGridProps> = ({
  products,
  onProductSelected,
  onAddToCart,
}) => {
  return (
    <div className="product-grid">
      {products.map((product) => (
        <ProductCard
          key={product.id}
          product={product}
          onSelected={onProductSelected}
          onAddToCart={onAddToCart}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

```typescript
// Components/Catalog/CatalogFilters.tsx
interface CatalogFiltersProps {
  categories: string[];
  onFiltersApplied: (filter: ProductFilter) => void;
  onFiltersCleared: () => void;
}

export const CatalogFilters: React.FC<CatalogFiltersProps> = ({
  categories,
  onFiltersApplied,
  onFiltersCleared,
}) => {
  const [selectedCategories, setSelectedCategories] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [priceRange, setPriceRange] = useState<[number, number]>([0, 1000]);

  const handleApplyFilters = () => {
    onFiltersApplied({
      categories: selectedCategories,
      priceRange,
    });
  };

  return (
    <div className="catalog-filters">
      <h3>Filters</h3>
      <div className="filter-group">
        <h4>Categories</h4>
        {categories.map((category) => (
          <label key={category}>
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={selectedCategories.includes(category)}
              onChange={(e) => {
                if (e.target.checked) {
                  setSelectedCategories([...selectedCategories, category]);
                } else {
                  setSelectedCategories(
                    selectedCategories.filter((c) => c !== category)
                  );
                }
              }}
            />
            {category}
          </label>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div className="filter-group">
        <h4>Price Range</h4>
        <input
          type="range"
          min="0"
          max="1000"
          value={priceRange[0]}
          onChange={(e) =>
            setPriceRange([Number(e.target.value), priceRange[1]])
          }
        />
        <input
          type="range"
          min="0"
          max="1000"
          value={priceRange[1]}
          onChange={(e) =>
            setPriceRange([priceRange[0], Number(e.target.value)])
          }
        />
        <span>
          ${priceRange[0]} - ${priceRange[1]}
        </span>
      </div>
      <button onClick={handleApplyFilters}>Apply Filters</button>
      <button onClick={onFiltersCleared}>Clear Filters</button>
    </div>
  );
};
```

